{
  "summary": "The analysis compared 18 budget‑to‑actual lines for August 2026, revealing a net unfavorable variance of $89,250.52. Seven lines are flagged ‘review’ (requiring immediate investigation), six are ‘notable’ (monitor closely), and five are ‘on track’. The largest drivers are GL 530000/CC‑20 (+$22,861), GL 520000/CC‑10 (+$11,364), GL 500000/CC‑30 (+$10,540), GL 530000/CC‑10 (+$9,750) and GL 510000/CC‑20 (+$8,224) – all in ‘review’ status. Additionally, several ‘notable’ lines carry materiality flags (e.g., GL 400000/CC‑10, GL 410000/CC‑10/CC‑20) and should be validated for timing or forecasting issues. No ‘exception’ items were identified, but the concentration of review‑status variances in cost centers CC‑10, CC‑20 and CC‑30 warrants focused follow‑up by the respective budget owners."
}

{
  "summary": "The Bank-to-GL reconciliation shows 41 compared transactions, all flagged as exceptions with no corresponding GL entries found. All 41 exceptions originate from the bank statement (e.g., INV-1000 to INV-1004) and carry full amount variances (e.g., $3,377.42 for INV-1000), indicating missing or unrecorded GL postings. Zero transactions matched automatically, and none require review beyond these exceptions. Immediate human investigation is needed to locate the missing GL entries, verify posting omissions, or identify timing differences for all 41 items. The total unreconciled amount across the sample exceeds $20,000, representing a material exposure requiring resolution before period close."
}
